  "answer": "The fix is in place. Let me confirm the behavior against the requirements:\n\n- **Non-string input** → `TypeError` (unchanged guard). ✓\n- **Empty/whitespace-only** → `trim()` yields `''`, `replace` leaves it `''`, `toLowerCase()` returns `''`. ✓\n- **Leading/trailing whitespace removed** → `trim()`. ✓\n- **Internal whitespace runs collapsed** → `replace(/\\s+/g, ' ')` after trimming, so only internal runs remain and each becomes one ASCII space. ✓\n- **Lowercasing via `String.prototype.toLowerCase()`** → `.toLowerCase()`. ✓\n- Named export `normalizeText` and public tests untouched. ✓\n\nThe change was a single-line edit to `normalize.mjs`:\n\n```js\nreturn value.trim().replace(/\\s+/g, ' ').toLowerCase();\n```\n\nThe original code only trimmed and lowercased, so internal runs of spaces/tabs/newlines were preserved. Adding `.replace(/\\s+/g, ' ')` between `trim()` and `toLowerCase()` collapses every nonempty internal whitespace run (spaces, tabs, line breaks, etc.) into a single ASCII space, matching the spec and the public tests.",
